{
	title: 'Claude subscriptions through the Agent SDK, one login folder per account',
	spec: "An Anthropic subscription account can be a Claude Code login folder instead of OAuth tokens held by Hal, and a user can have several. `/login claude-sdk <name>` creates <home>/secrets/claude-sdk/<name>/ (0700) and tells the user to sign in with Claude Code's own /login there (CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR=<folder> claude), so Hal never collects, reads or stores subscription tokens. Each folder is one account in auth.all beside OAuth and API-key accounts. It gets the same pickAccount ranking, /status usage windows and rotation (tasks 61, wf, 3g), and a session stays on its account for the prompt cache. A turn on such an account runs through @anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk query() with env CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR=<folder>. Hal's system prompt replaces Claude Code's (custom systemPrompt), Claude Code's built-in tools are off, and Hal's native tool is an in-process SDK MCP server, so the model sees the same prompt and tool as on the direct path. History, rounds naming the account (task 2yf), usage and errors are recorded as for direct requests; a Claude Code failure reaches the user complete. One Claude Code process runs per active turn and exits when it ends. API keys keep the direct path. Why: Anthropic allows a user's own subscription in the unmodified Claude Code binary and the Agent SDK for personal use, but not a third-party product that offers claude.ai login or collects, stores or intermediates its tokens. Shipping this path to other users still needs Anthropic's approval; until then it is for personal use.",
	status: 'planned',
	needs: ['61', 'wf', 'nd', '29', '2yf']
}
